## Building on two previous summits

The [first RdRp Summit](/summits/rdrp-summit-2023/), held in Valencia in 2023, brought together more than 70 participants from over 50 research institutions, with a high representation of early career researchers. The [second](/summits/rdrp-summit-2025/), held in Lisbon in 2025, was supported by ISME, which funded travel grants for early career researchers.

Each summit produced a published community consensus statement: [2023, Frontiers in Virology](https://doi.org/10.3389/fviro.2024.1371958) and [2025, Peer Community Journal](https://doi.org/10.24072/pcjournal.727).

Between summits, the community runs the [RNA Virus Journal Club](/journal-club/) and open working groups on benchmarking, phylogeny, and host-virus interactions.

## What will be added

The programme, invited speakers, registration, abstract deadlines, and fees are being worked out by the organising committee. This page will be updated as each is confirmed. For announcements, follow the community Slack or [Bluesky](https://bsky.app/profile/rdrpsummit.bsky.social).
